{"name":"Illuminating Experience","hex":"#dee4e0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"illuminating","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Providing illumination or light.","Providing clarification or explanation; educational, revealing."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of illuminate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/illuminating"},{"term":"experience","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The effect upon the judgment or feelings produced by any event, whether witnessed or participated in; personal and direct impressions as contrasted with description or fancies; personal acquaintance; actual enjoyment or suffering.","An activity one has performed."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To observe certain events; undergo a certain feeling or process; or perform certain actions that may alter one or contribute to one's knowledge, opinions, or skills."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/experience"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lighting","blocks":[{"text":"Lighting or illumination is the deliberate use of light to achieve practical or aesthetic effects. Lighting includes the use of both artificial light sources like lamps and light fixtures, as well as natural illumination by capturing daylight. Daylighting is sometimes used as the main source of light during daytime in buildings. This can save energy in place of using artificial lighting, which represents a major component of energy consumption in buildings. Proper lighting can enhance task performance, improve the appearance of an area, or have positive psychological effects on occupants."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Acropolis_Of_Athens_Greece_04.jpg/330px-Acropolis_Of_Athens_Greece_04.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lighting","wikidata":"Q210064"},{"title":"Experience","blocks":[{"text":"Experience refers to conscious events in general, more specifically to perceptions, or to the practical knowledge and familiarity that is produced by these processes. Understood as a conscious event in the widest sense, experience involves a subject to which various items are presented. In this sense, seeing a yellow bird on a branch presents the subject with the objects \"bird\" and \"branch\", the relation between them and the property \"yellow\". Unreal items may be included as well, which happens when experiencing hallucinations or dreams. When understood in a more restricted sense, only sensory consciousness counts as experience. In this sense, experience is usually identified with perception and contrasted with other types of conscious events, like thinking or imagining. In a slightly different sense, experience refers not to the conscious events themselves but to the practical knowledge and familiarity they produce. Hence, it is important that direct perceptual contact with the external world is the source of knowledge. So an experienced hiker is someone who has actually lived through many hikes, not someone who merely read many books about hiking. This is associated both with recurrent past acquaintance and the abilities learned through them."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Experience","wikidata":"Q164359"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Cherry_blossoms_with_Isuzu-Chaya_and_Akafuku_store_at_Night.jpg/500px-Cherry_blossoms_with_Isuzu-Chaya_and_Akafuku_store_at_Night.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Cherry_blossoms_with_Isuzu-Chaya_and_Akafuku_store_at_Night.jpg/1280px-Cherry_blossoms_with_Isuzu-Chaya_and_Akafuku_store_at_Night.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Cherry_blossoms_with_Isuzu-Chaya_and_Akafuku_store_at_Night.jpg/500px-Cherry_blossoms_with_Isuzu-Chaya_and_Akafuku_store_at_Night.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Illuminated cherry blossoms, light from the shop windows, and Japanese lantern at night in Ise, Mie, Japan","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACherry_blossoms_with_Isuzu-Chaya_and_Akafuku_store_at_Night.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/2012_%EA%B2%BD%EB%B3%B5%EA%B6%81_%EA%B2%BD%ED%9A%8C%EB%A3%A8_%EC%95%BC%EA%B0%84%EA%B0%9C%EC%9E%A5.jpg/500px-2012_%EA%B2%BD%EB%B3%B5%EA%B6%81_%EA%B2%BD%ED%9A%8C%EB%A3%A8_%EC%95%BC%EA%B0%84%EA%B0%9C%EC%9E%A5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/2012_%EA%B2%BD%EB%B3%B5%EA%B6%81_%EA%B2%BD%ED%9A%8C%EB%A3%A8_%EC%95%BC%EA%B0%84%EA%B0%9C%EC%9E%A5.jpg/500px-2012_%EA%B2%BD%EB%B3%B5%EA%B6%81_%EA%B2%BD%ED%9A%8C%EB%A3%A8_%EC%95%BC%EA%B0%84%EA%B0%9C%EC%9E%A5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The lights illuminating Gyeonghoeru at Gyeongbokgung Palace in Seoul, Korea","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2012_%EA%B2%BD%EB%B3%B5%EA%B6%81_%EA%B2%BD%ED%9A%8C%EB%A3%A8_%EC%95%BC%EA%B0%84%EA%B0%9C%EC%9E%A5.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Finland%2C_Porvoo%2C_Old_Town_by_night%2C_Teemu_Eskola.jpg/500px-Finland%2C_Porvoo%2C_Old_Town_by_night%2C_Teemu_Eskola.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Finland%2C_Porvoo%2C_Old_Town_by_night%2C_Teemu_Eskola.jpg/1280px-Finland%2C_Porvoo%2C_Old_Town_by_night%2C_Teemu_Eskola.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Finland%2C_Porvoo%2C_Old_Town_by_night%2C_Teemu_Eskola.jpg/500px-Finland%2C_Porvoo%2C_Old_Town_by_night%2C_Tee